56.6929133858267775 629.291574803149615 Td
(As e-commerce websites expand rapidly, consumers are confronted with limited ability to find the best deals based on) Tj
11.4115384615384894 Tw
0. -9.7749999999999986 Td
(fragmented prices, concealed shipping fees, uncertain delivery periods, and seller reliability inconsistency. Current price) Tj
6.3575000000000186 Tw
0. -9.7749999999999986 Td
(comparison systems mainly rely on the cheapest sticker price, ignoring other factors that affect the ultimate buying decision. This) Tj
5.340681818181837 Tw
0. -9.7749999999999986 Td
(paper introduces Price Vision AI, a system powered by AI that allows users to upload an image of a product, identify the product) Tj
11.2840909090909562 Tw
0. -9.7749999999999986 Td
(automatically using vision-language models \(CLIP/BLIP\), normalize product information, retrieve up-to-date pricing information) Tj
6.7919444444444581 Tw
0. -9.7749999999999986 Td
(from large online marketplaces \(Flipkart, Amazon\), and calculate the actual best offer by taking into account final price, coupon) Tj
7.8375000000000181 Tw
0. -9.7749999999999986 Td
(discount, delivery time, shipping fees, and seller reputation. The system is built with FastAPI \(backend\), Playwright \(scraping\),) Tj
9.5088461538461768 Tw
0. -9.7749999999999986 Td
(React \(frontend\), and Redis/Postgres \(data management\). The most important features are watchlists, price-drop notifications,) Tj
8.5470000000000201 Tw
0. -9.7749999999999986 Td
(and historical price trending. Experimental testing shows high recognition accuracy of products \(>90%\), quick response times) Tj
0 Tw
0. -9.7749999999999986 Td
(\(<= 6s p95 for two-source comparisons\), and stable error handling.) Tj
